prompt:
Create a replacement production sprite atlas of articulated trouser legs and boots for the three game characters in the references. Match the references' high resolution painted 1990s arcade action game style, the exact saturated blue trousers, red trousers, olive enemy trousers, heavy black combat boots, confident dark outline and controlled painterly fabric highlights.

DELIVERABLE: transparent PNG portrait atlas, 1536 by 2048 or a proportional portrait size. Exactly 3 equal columns and 6 equal rows, generous transparent gutters, no text, no grids, no floor, no shadows outside each part. Column 1 blue, column 2 red, column 3 olive. Each column contains exactly:
row 1 near upper leg/thigh, hip to knee only;
row 2 near lower leg/shin, knee to ankle only, WITHOUT any boot;
row 3 complete near combat boot, including shaft, heel, sole and full toe pointing RIGHT;
row 4 far upper leg/thigh, hip to knee only;
row 5 far lower leg/shin, knee to ankle only, WITHOUT any boot;
row 6 complete far combat boot, including shaft, heel, sole and full toe pointing RIGHT.

CRITICAL GEOMETRY: These are neutral rigging pieces, not running poses. All thigh and shin pieces have perfectly straight vertical anatomical axes, their upper and lower joint centers aligned at the same x. No bent thighs, no S curves, no hip flare, no bent knee or diagonal limb. Both ends have short rounded overlapping caps with no black line drawn across the joint opening. The upper thighs are muscular and broad, width about 60 percent of the hip-to-knee distance; the shins width about 44 percent of the knee-to-ankle distance. Realistic taper only, no skinny tube legs. Keep joint-to-joint lengths of thigh and shin equal throughout this atlas. Near and far pieces use identical anatomy and source scale. Far pieces are only slightly darker, not smaller. Cargo seams and pockets follow the reference, do not paint kneecaps twice. The shin ends at the ankle and may overlap the upper boot shaft; the boot contains the entire ankle and foot as ONE complete independently rotatable piece. Boots must be substantial, about as wide toe-to-heel as 75 percent of a thigh's joint-to-joint length. Ankle shaft is upright, sole horizontal. Identical proportions and alignment for all three palette columns. Keep every separate piece entirely inside its own cell with ample margins. Do not include any torsos, belts spanning both hips, weapons, labels, human heads or backgrounds.
